# The published analyses verify their plan by the SHA-256 of the file's bytes and refuse to run if it has
# changed since the rules were fixed. Git's own line-ending conversion is such a change: with
# core.autocrlf=true, which is the default on Windows installs, a fresh clone writes these files with CRLF
# and every plan-pinned script stops with "the plan has changed since the rules were fixed". Checked by
# cloning this repository on 2026-10-21, where all three plans hashed to values none of the scripts expect.
# These paths are therefore never converted, in either direction.
docs/plans/*.md -text
